{"units": [{"id": "dyspotmos-quote5", "translation": "to the ill-fated cow."}, {"id": "dyspotmos_adv-orth1", "translation": "unfortunately"}, {"id": "dyspotmos_adv-def1", "translation": "unfortunately"}, {"id": "dyspotmos_adv-quote1", "translation": "of the dead who perished miserably."}, {"id": "dyspotos-orth1", "translation": "not drinkable"}, {"id": "dyspotos-def1", "translation": "not drinkable"}, {"id": "dyspotos-quote1", "translation": "may I carry food of a drink that is not drinkable."}, {"id": "dysprageo-orth1", "translation": "to be unfortunate"}, {"id": "dysprageo-def1", "translation": "I am unfortunate"}, {"id": "dysprageo-quote1", "translation": "to groan for the one who is unfortunate."}, {"id": "dyspraxia-orth1", "translation": "misfortune"}, {"id": "dyspraxia-def1", "translation": "misery"}, {"id": "dyspraxia-quote1", "translation": "my misfortune."}, {"id": "dyspraxia-quote2", "translation": "with helpless misfortunes."}, {"id": "dyssebeia-orth1", "translation": "impiety"}, {"id": "dyssebeia-def1", "translation": "impiety"}, {"id": "dyssebeia-quote1", "translation": "this was in my mind as impiety."}, {"id": "dyssebeo-orth1", "translation": "to be impious"}, {"id": "dyssebeo-def1", "translation": "I am impious"}, {"id": "dyssebeo-quote1", "translation": "may you be more hateful than the impious."}, {"id": "dyssebes-orth1", "translation": "impious"}, {"id": "dyssebes-def1", "translation": "impious"}, {"id": "dyssebes-quote1", "translation": "to the more impious ones."}, {"id": "dyssebes-quote2", "translation": "breathing impious turning of the mind."}, {"id": "dyssebes-quote3", "translation": "for the impious deed begets more after it."}, {"id": "dyssebia-orth1", "translation": "impiety"}, {"id": "dyssebia-def1", "translation": "impiety"}, {"id": "dyssebia-quote1", "translation": "insolence is the child of impiety."}, {"id": "dystekmartos-orth1", "translation": "hard to discern"}, {"id": "dystekmartos-def1", "translation": "difficult to understand"}, {"id": "dystekmartos-quote1", "translation": "I pushed mortals into a craft hard to discern."}, {"id": "dysterpes-orth1", "translation": "unpleasant"}, {"id": "dysterpes-def1", "translation": "unpleasant"}, {"id": "dysterpes-quote1", "translation": "many unpleasant evils."}, {"id": "dystenos-orth1", "translation": "wretched"}, {"id": "dystenos-def1", "translation": "wretched"}, {"id": "dystenos-note1", "translation": "(No examples of the Doric form δύστανος [wretched] are found in Aeschylus: for δυστάνων [of the wretched], which is read in M Sept. 999, is corrupted from δυστόνων [of the ill-sounding].)"}, {"id": "dystenos-quote1", "translation": "wretched"}, {"id": "dystenos-quote2", "translation": "of the wretched"}, {"id": "dystenos-quote3", "translation": "of the ill-sounding"}, {"id": "dystenos-quote4", "translation": "I was held by dreams, wretched."}, {"id": "dystenos-quote5", "translation": "from a wretched father."}, {"id": "dystenos-quote6", "translation": "I have long been silent, wretched."}, {"id": "dystenos-quote7", "translation": "they butcher the limbs of the wretched."}, {"id": "dystenos-quote8", "translation": "Alas, wretched me."}, {"id": "dystenos-quote9", "translation": "the wretched army of the Argives."}, {"id": "dystenos-quote10", "translation": "wretched harvest."}, {"id": "dystenos-quote11", "translation": "a wretched, miserable dove being fed."}, {"id": "dystletos-orth1", "translation": "hard to bear"}, {"id": "dystletos-def1", "translation": "hard to bear"}, {"id": "dystletos-quote1", "translation": "to love these things, hard to bear though they are."}, {"id": "dystonos-orth1", "translation": "lamentable"}, {"id": "dystonos-def1", "translation": "lamentable"}, {"id": "dystonos-note1", "translation": "The verse is faulty: for an iambic dimeter is required, such as I restored by uncertain conjecture: dύστανος ἀ κηδεμονία [wretched the care]."}, {"id": "dystonos-note2", "translation": "where δυστόνων [of the ill-sounding] is restored from the apograph in place of δυστάνων [of the wretched], which is in M."}, {"id": "dystonos-quote1", "translation": "lamentable cares of the same name."}, {"id": "dystonos-quote2", "translation": "wretched the care"}, {"id": "dystonos-quote3", "translation": "Alas, alas, of ill-sounding evils,"}, {"id": "dystonos-quote4", "translation": "of the ill-sounding"}, {"id": "dystonos-quote5", "translation": "of the wretched"}, {"id": "dystonos-quote6", "translation": "Alas, lamentable, unbearable cares."}, {"id": "dystycheo-orth1", "translation": "to be unfortunate"}, {"id": "dystycheo-def1", "translation": "I am unfortunate"}, {"id": "dystycheo-quote1", "translation": "if I am unfortunate."}, {"id": "dystycheo-quote2", "translation": "you neglect yourself when you are unfortunate."}, {"id": "dystycheo-quote3", "translation": "I pray that he may prosper, but these may be unfortunate."}, {"id": "dystycheo-quote4", "translation": "and for the unfortunate, release is easy."}, {"id": "dystyches-orth1", "translation": "unfortunate"}, {"id": "dystyches-def1", "translation": "unfortunate"}, {"id": "dystyches-quote1", "translation": "many things—and he fares unfortunately."}, {"id": "dystyches-quote2", "translation": "for having borne me, you cast me into misfortune."}, {"id": "dystyches-quote3", "translation": "great indeed are the unfortunate maidens."}, {"id": "dystychos-orth1", "translation": "unfortunately"}, {"id": "dystychos-def1", "translation": "unfortunately"}, {"id": "dystychos-quote1", "translation": "struck unfortunately by the heavy bile of the deity."}, {"id": "dysphatos-orth1", "translation": "ill-omened"}, {"id": "dysphatos-def1", "translation": "unspeakable"}, {"id": "dysphatos-quote1", "translation": "with ill-omened cry."}, {"id": "dysphemeo-orth1", "translation": "to speak ill-omened words"}, {"id": "dysphemeo-def1", "translation": "I speak ill-omened words"}, {"id": "dysphemeo-quote1", "translation": "she calls the god with ill-omened words."}, {"id": "dysphiles-orth1", "translation": "hateful"}, {"id": "dysphiles-def1", "translation": "hateful"}, {"id": "dysphiles-quote1", "translation": "hateful beast."}, {"id": "dysphiles-quote2", "translation": "the hateful famine dwelling with darkness."}, {"id": "dysphiles-quote3", "translation": "hateful marriage."}, {"id": "dysphiles-quote4", "translation": "for no one honors what is hateful to the gods."}, {"id": "dysphiles-quote5", "translation": "from their eyes they drip hateful blood."}, {"id": "dysphiles-quote6", "translation": "from their eyes they pour a hateful stream."}, {"id": "dysphoreo-orth1", "translation": "to bear with difficulty"}, {"id": "dysphoreo-def1", "translation": "I bear with difficulty"}, {"id": "dysphoreo-quote1", "translation": "grieving over pain."}, {"id": "dysphoreo-quote2", "translation": "it is no wonder to be distressed by fear in the mind."}, {"id": "dysphoros-orth1", "translation": "hard to bear"}, {"id": "dysphoros-def1", "translation": "hard to bear"}, {"id": "dysphoros-note1", "translation": "where prodύσφορον [hard to bear], which conflicts with the meter, M. Schmidt conjectured ἄφερτον [unbearable]."}, {"id": "dysphoros-quote1", "translation": "a more grievous lament."}, {"id": "dysphoros-quote2", "translation": "I will tell of my own hard-to-bear life."}, {"id": "dysphoros-quote3", "translation": "hard-to-bear ruin."}, {"id": "dysphoros-quote4", "translation": "hard-to-bear insolence,"}, {"id": "dysphoros-quote5", "translation": "hard to bear on ship and on land."}, {"id": "dysphoros-word1", "translation": "hard to bear"}, {"id": "dysphoros-word2", "translation": "unbearable"}, {"id": "dysphronos-orth1", "translation": "unwisely"}, {"id": "dysphronos-note1", "translation": "where since neither the meaning of rash nor of malevolent is suitable, I conjectured δυσφόρως [with difficulty]."}, {"id": "dysphronos-quote1", "translation": "Xerxes followed all things unwisely,"}, {"id": "dysphronos-word1", "translation": "with difficulty"}, {"id": "dysphronis-orth1", "translation": "of ill mind, sad"}, {"id": "dysphronis-def1", "translation": "whose mind is ill, sad"}, {"id": "dysphronis-def2", "translation": "malevolent, hostile"}, {"id": "dysphronis-def3", "translation": "imprudent"}, {"id": "dysphronis-quote1", "translation": "from where did this ill-minded hatred come upon the army?"}, {"id": "dysphronis-quote2", "translation": "hostile to the ill-minded."}, {"id": "dysphronis-quote3", "translation": "for an ill-minded arrow sits upon the heart."}, {"id": "dysphronis-quote4", "translation": "soothing charms of the ill-minded."}]}